extends RefCounted
## Every weapon's stats in one place. Tweak the numbers here; nothing else
## needs to change. The order of LIST is the weapon slot order (keys 1-8).
##
## Fields:
##  name            shown on the HUD and in pickup messages
##  model           the gun model for pickups, the rack and the Armory (Medium detail;
##                  barrel along +X, grip at the origin, real size in metres)
##  view_model      first-person model: assets/models/guns/<view_model>_<low|med|high>.glb,
##                  picked by graphics quality (tools/blender/build_guns.py)
##  hold            hand poses (weapon_view.gd HOLDS): "pistol" / "handgun" (both hands on the
##                  grip), "rifle" (left hand under the handguard), "shotgun" (pump)
##  left_hand       where the left palm holds the gun, gun space (m: +X barrel, +Y up, +Z right)
##  hip             where the grip sits at the hip, view space (m, before
##                  player.gd VIEW_SCALE; +X right, -Z forward)
##  ads_distance    eye to grip (m) while aiming down the sights
##  sight_height    sight line above the grip (m); 0 = measured from the model at sight_at
##  port            ejection port, gun space (spent casings come out here)
##  casing          spent casing: "pistol", "rifle", "shell" or "" (none)
##  pickup_length   size of the floating pickup in the arena, in metres
##  (which weapons you start with, and the others' shop prices, are in economy.gd)
##  move_scale      walking / running speed while holding it (1 = normal)
##  automatic       true = hold to keep firing, false = one shot per press
##  damage          per bullet (enemies have 3 HP)
##  pellets         bullets per shot (shotgun > 1)
##  spread          random spread cone in degrees (always applied)
##  spread_per_shot extra spread added by each shot while firing (recoil bloom)
##  max_spread      cap for that extra spread
##  spread_recovery how fast the extra spread shrinks again, degrees per second
##  range           how far bullets reach, metres
##  mag_size        rounds per magazine
##  reserve         spare rounds you get with the weapon (-1 = unlimited)
##  max_reserve     most spare rounds you can carry (-1 = unlimited)
##  ammo_box        spare rounds one ammo box gives this weapon
##  fire_delay      seconds between shots (includes the pump / bolt time)
##  cycle_sound     pump or bolt sound played after each shot (null = none)
##  cycle_delay     seconds after the shot before the pump / bolt sound
##  reload_time     seconds
##  reload_sounds   [[seconds after reload starts, sound], ...]
##  shot_sound, shot_volume_db
##  shot_pitch      base pitch of the shot sound (1 = as recorded)
##  recoil          how hard the gun model kicks back
##  view_kick       how many degrees the view climbs per shot
##  shake           camera shake per shot (0..1)
##  flash_size      muzzle flash scale
##  zoom_fov        scope field of view while aiming (0 = no scope)
##  scoped_spread   spread while scoped (replaces `spread`)
##  sight           what aiming looks through: "iron" (the top of the gun),
##                  "red_dot" (a reflex sight added on top) or "scope" (the
##                  sniper: full-screen scope overlay, uses zoom_fov)
##  ads_fov         field of view while aiming down the sights (not "scope")
##  ads_spread      spread multiplier while aiming down the sights (0.5 = half)
##  sight_at        where along the gun the front sight sits, 0 = back .. 1 = muzzle
##  ads_offset      extra nudge (m) for the gun while aiming, if a hand is in the way
##
## Optional first-person fields (only the Pistol sets them; see player.gd):
##  arms            fp_arms.gd model: "arms" (default) or "gloves" (hands + short sleeves)
##  arms_scale      size of that model; arms_shoulders: where its shoulders sit (fp_arms.gd)
##  view_scale      player.gd ViewModel scale (default VIEW_SCALE): smaller = less wall clipping
##  view_fov        FOV the gun and arms are drawn with; ads_view_fov while aiming
##  ads_drop        sights this far (m) below the screen centre (default ADS_SIGHT_DROP)
##  breath          idle breathing sway / walk roll amount (0 = none)
##  recoil_spring   true = the kick springs back (snappy) instead of fading out
##  recoil_back, recoil_pitch   kick per unit of recoil (default RECOIL_BACK / RECOIL_PITCH)
##  holster         [position, rotation in degrees] of WeaponReload when switched out / in
##  reload_sounds entries may end with "empty": only played when reloading an empty gun

